From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 09:29:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] [VectraOS] RISC-V: the Swift calling convention (stage 1)

llvm-project#213448 (both commits, as of 2026-08-13), backported to the
Swift 6.4.0 pin: clang accepts swiftcall on riscv (not the E ABIs) and
keeps refusing swiftasynccall; the backend passes swiftself in x20 (s4),
returns up to four values in a0-a3/fa0-fa3, and won't tail call when an
argument in a callee-saved register isn't the caller's own. Pinned
CC_RISCV has no CC_RISCV_Impl yet, so the CallingConv hunk is applied by
hand. swifterror stays in memory (SwiftErrorInRegister false).
